# Generated by pipeline/build-react.mjs, which emits each icon's presentation
# attributes on one line. Prettier explodes them onto seven, which is a 3800
# line diff that `npm run icons:react:check` then reports as drift: the file no
# longer matches what the generator would write, so `npm run icons:ci` fails on
# a repo where the only thing anyone did was run `npm run format`. Formatting
# this file is not a style choice the repo gets to make. The generator owns it.
#
# Both targets, for the same reason. The generator writes them byte-identical,
# so formatting one and not the other would put them permanently out of sync
# with each other as well as with the generator.
components/icons/index.tsx
packages/*/src/*.tsx

# Generated by pipeline/build-github-registry.mjs. Same trap as the React
# modules: formatting one file makes it disagree with its generator, and the
# GitHub registry then ships a different drawing than `/r/{name}.json`.
registry.json
registry/

# Generated by pipeline/build-history.mjs, minified: it is imported by the
# page, so every newline in it is payload. Prettier would expand it and `history:check` would report drift.
lib/icon-history.json

# Not generated, but parsed. `pipeline/check-readmes.mjs` finds each count with
# a regex that expects single spaces around the table pipes, and Prettier pads
# those columns to align them. The result is three MISSING counts on a repo
# where all anyone did was run `npm run format`, and the failure names the
# numbers rather than the formatting, so it reads as a stale count. The tables
# are hand-aligned and stay that way.
README.md
pipeline/README.md
raw/README.md
packages/*/README.md
